  "reasoning": "Octopuses indeed have three hearts and blue blood. Two branchial hearts pump blood through the gills to pick up oxygen, while a third systemic heart pumps oxygenated blood throughout the rest of the body. Furthermore, octopus blood is blue because it relies on the copper-rich protein hemocyanin rather than iron-based hemoglobin to transport oxygen in cold, low-oxygen marine environments.",
